{"id": "EUVD-2026-107358", "enisaUuid": "491ec92d-ff46-3f3b-a924-48b584e2eb2d", "description": "A vulnerability in the control channel socket implementation of&nbsp;Open Source Snort 3 could allow an authenticated, local attacker with low privileges to execute arbitrary commands as the Snort 3 process user.\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability is due to a lack of authentication when a local user connects to the Snort control channel socket. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by connecting to the Snort 3 control channel socket as a local user. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to execute arbitrary commands as well as read and write Snort 3 process memory.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T16:18:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T13:37:52", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://sec.cloudapps.cisco.com/security/center/content/CiscoSecurityAdvisory/cisco-sa-opensrc-snort3-2fXGJPfe"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-76524", "GHSA-4376-j46p-qqm7"], "assigner": "cisco", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "003f1953-e393-3199-8659-32e8133ad6bf", "product": {"name": "Cisco Open Source Snort3", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.1.16.0"}, {"id": "0204b639-1aad-3f65-ae02-90334fd075d7", "product": {"name": "Cisco Open Source Snort3", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.1.59.0"}, {"id": "051475b7-b717-36e2-a592-14ba7855b973", "product": {"name": "Cisco Open Source Snort3", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.1.69.0"}, {"id": "05293235-f286-3f1f-b7f3-463e0f9fd01f", "product": {"name": "Cisco Open Source Snort3", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.9.7.0"}, {"id": "09a0cbb4-8140-3b14-8838-90e4e840bf52", "product": {"name": "Cisco Open Source Snort3", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.1.19.0"}, {"id": "09f65356-c662-37a8-b0e6-d3da4e99624d", "product": {"name": "Cisco Open Source Snort3", "vendor": {"name"